 "description": "FULL AUTONOMY (jabberwock's design): the never-satisfying UNDERSTAND drive's standing error, wired through mint/select/satisfy rules into the goal machinery, mints the next hill forever via the prose->action faculty. frontier_pick MIGRATED to graph data; plan-algebra (Fix/Branch/While/Seq) admissible for the [V2] execute reflex. goal_from_procedure CONSUMES plan_root->goaled_root at mint so a satisfied goal's drop isn't fought by a re-mint (clean graph-data sidestep of a rule-engine add/del-same-edge interaction); rearm_on_reset restores plan_root for penalty-free retry.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "autonomy",
  "description": "perceive -> understand -> mint goals -> pursue (prose->action) -> learn (confirm/refute via reset) -> re-mint; the understand drive's error never reaches zero."
 },
